From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:49:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(inventory): confirm survival offhand transfers from
 Bedrock

Bedrock 2193 rejects Java item stack requests involving the offhand and a cursor created by a legacy offhand take. Use normal inventory transactions for both directions and for placing that cursor into an empty player inventory slot. Wait for the authoritative offhand or inventory update before changing the Java cursor, and reopen inventory for recovery when confirmation times out. Keep unsupported clicks on the synthetic cursor from sending requests that the server cannot validate.
